                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Consolidating theoretical knowledge and forming a teaching model that combines theory with practice and supplements each other through clinical operations can enable students to independently receive patients, make clear diagnoses and treatment plans. According to common diseases in prosthodontics, including tooth preparation and impression taking for fixed, removable and complete dentures, etc., it can stimulate students' enthusiasm and initiative, combine theory with practice, and improve the internship effect. At the same time, it can exercise students' ability to solve practical problems, establish the quality of "patient-centered", love for the job, and the will to calmly analyze and deal with problems when encountering them.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
